{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And after that came forth his brother, and his hand was holding the heel of Esau.</b> For the hand of his dominion would not be his immediately on the day of his birth, but only at the end, when his days were advanced, in accordance with the indication of the name עָקֵב, which points to the end. So too, spiritual perfection is acquired more fully at the end of a man's days, for ״סוֹף כָּל דָּבָר הַכֹּל נִשְׁמָע״ (Ecclesiastes 12:13), and the elders among the disciples of the sages increase in wisdom. But on the day of his birth there is no trace at all of that spiritual perfection — and if so, one is compelled to say that there is no reward for the righteous in this world, since the principal time for the acquisition of perfection is in the days of old age, when one is near the gates of death, for then his intellect grows ever stronger. And when will he receive his reward? For the days of old age are not suited to receive the reward, since all desires have already ceased in him — ״וְתָפֵר הָאֲבִיּוֹנָה״ (Ecclesiastes 12:5). If so, perforce you must say that the hand of the perfected ones holds the heel of Esau, that is, the end of the dominion of Esau." "<b>And his hand was holding the heel of Esau.</b> This was a sign that in the future Esau would despise the birthright as something a person tramples under his heels and treats with contempt, and in that very heel Jacob would take hold — that is, what Esau trampled under his heel, Jacob would grasp. And so too all the light commandments that people trample under their heels — the Satan keeps count against them — Jacob will take hold of and fulfill. And the word עָקֵב also serves to mean עָקְבָה (deceit) and מִרְמָה (trickery), to tell you that Jacob seized upon him from the side of Esau being a deceiver and a trapper, with all his deeds done in deceit and trickery; therefore he is not fit to be the firstborn, for the service of HaShem, blessed be He, belonged to the firstborn. Therefore Jacob grasped him by his heel in order to restrain him, so that he would not emerge first, as Rashi explained — that Jacob came to restrain him, that he might be first for the birth, etc. And for this reason he grasped him specifically by his heel, for ״אָרוּר עֹשֶׂה מְלֶאכֶת ה׳ רְמִיָּה״ (Jeremiah 48:10) — in deceit and trickery, and this is a proper allusion." "<b>And he called his name Jacob.</b> And concerning Esau it says ״וַיִּקְרְאוּ שְׁמוֹ עֵשָׂו״ (Genesis 25:25) — they called his name Esau — for many called him Esau, because the evil paths are many and the good path is only one; therefore there were many who agreed upon the name of Esau. However, concerning Jacob, none would agree save the unique individuals of the generation and men of distinction, for those who attain ascent are few. And you already know that the name Esau points to the acquisitions of this world, which were already made and completed at the moment of his birth, as explained above (Genesis 25:25). And the name Jacob points to spiritual perfection acquired at the end; therefore concerning Esau it says ״וַיִּקְרְאוּ״ (they called) and concerning Jacob ״וַיִּקְרָא״ (he called) — and it is easy to understand."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:30:11.668069726Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}